@.str.260 = private unnamed_addr constant [20 x i8] c"search for packages\00", align 1
@.str.261 = private unnamed_addr constant [2552 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Show all packages in the `nixpkgs` flake:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix search nixpkgs ^\0A  * legacyPackages.x86_64-linux.AMB-plugins (0.8.1)\0A    A set of ambisonics ladspa plugins\0A\0A  * legacyPackages.x86_64-linux.ArchiSteamFarm (4.3.1.0)\0A    Application with primary purpose of idling Steam cards from multiple accounts simultaneously\0A  \E2\80\A6\0A  ```\0A\0A* Show packages in the `nixpkgs` flake containing `blender` in its\0A  name or description:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix search nixpkgs blender\0A  * legacyPackages.x86_64-linux.blender (2.91.0)\0A    3D Creation/Animation/Publishing System\0A  ```\0A\0A* Search for packages underneath the attribute `gnome3` in Nixpkgs:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix search nixpkgs#gnome3 vala\0A  * legacyPackages.x86_64-linux.gnome3.vala (0.48.9)\0A    Compiler for GObject type system\0A  ```\0A\0A* Show all packages in the flake in the current directory:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix search . ^\0A  ```\0A\0A* Search for Firefox or Chromium:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix search nixpkgs 'firefox|chromium'\0A  ```\0A\0A* Search for packages containing `git` and either `frontend` or `gui`:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix search nixpkgs git 'frontend|gui'\0A  ```\0A\0A* Search for packages containing `neovim` but hide ones containing either `gui` or `python`:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix search nixpkgs neovim --exclude 'python|gui'\0A  ```\0A  or\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix search nixpkgs neovim --exclude 'python' --exclude 'gui'\0A  ```\0A\0A# Description\0A\0A`nix search` searches [*installable*](./nix.md#installables) (which can be evaluated, that is, a\0Aflake or Nix expression, but not a store path or store derivation path) for packages whose name or description matches all of the\0Aregular expressions *regex*. For each matching package, It prints the\0Afull attribute name (from the root of the [installable](./nix.md#installables)), the version\0Aand the `meta.description` field, highlighting the substrings that\0Awere matched by the regular expressions.\0A\0ATo show all packages, use the regular expression `^`. In contrast to `.*`,\0Ait avoids highlighting the entire name and description of every package.\0A\0A> Note that in this context, `^` is the regex character to match the beginning of a string, *not* the delimiter for\0A> [selecting a derivation output](@docroot@/command-ref/new-cli/nix.md#derivation-output-selection).\0A\0A# Flake output attributes\0A\0AIf no flake output attribute is given, `nix search` searches for\0Apackages:\0A\0A* Directly underneath `packages.<system>`.\0A\0A* Underneath `legacyPackages.<system>`, recursing into attribute sets\0A  that contain an attribute `recurseForDerivations = true`.\0A\0A\00", align 1
